{# pdns-backend-ldap: PowerDNS LDAP Backend Schema Definition
#
# This template generates an LDIF-compatible schema definition file for the
# pdns-backend-ldap PowerDNS module. It defines the LDAP object classes and
# attribute types required to store and retrieve DNS zones.
#
# This file is intended to be loaded into the LDAP directory (e.g., via ldapadd)
# once, or maintained idempotently. It does NOT configure the running daemon
# (which is done via pdns.conf or environment variables).
#
# Since this is a static schema definition, no dynamic runtime variables are
# injected into the directives themselves. However, comments are enriched to
# explain each attribute's purpose, OID, and RFC reference.
#}

# {# A schema for storing DNS zones in LDAP #}
# {# ORDERING is not necessary, and some servers don't support integerOrderingMatch. #}
